msgid "Practical near-term quantum computing"
msgstr "실용적인 근미래 양자 컴퓨팅"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "개요 {#overview}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/practical-near-term-qc/hero.svg)\n"
msgstr "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/practical-near-term-qc/hero.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-24
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course explores some of the most promising applications of quantum computing, including Hamiltonian simulation, optimization, machine learning, and differential equations. Each application is introduced through its theoretical motivation and then explored through hands-on case studies. We examine how real-world problems are mapped to quantum computers, which quantum techniques they use, and what evidence is needed to assess their potential.\n"
msgstr "이 과정에서는 해밀토니안 시뮬레이션, 최적화, 머신러닝, 미분 방정식 등 양자 컴퓨팅의 가장 유망한 응용 분야 일부를 살펴봅니다. 각 응용은 이론적 동기와 함께 소개한 뒤 실습 사례 연구를 통해 탐구합니다. 실제 문제가 양자 컴퓨터에 어떻게 매핑되는지, 어떤 양자 기법을 사용하는지, 그리고 그 잠재력을 평가하려면 어떤 근거가 필요한지 살펴봅니다.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exam {#exam}"
